#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cosh_integral

#% text
# `cosh_integral(x)` gives the hyperbolic cosine integral `Chi(x)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `Chi(x)` is `euler_gamma + log(x)` plus the integral of `(cosh(t) - 1)/t` from 0 to `x` (DLMF 6.2.16), for `x > 0`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values; a negative real argument gives a complex value.

#% item
# `cosh_integral` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cosh_integral(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8378669409802082

#% cell
cosh_integral(0.1)
#% output
#= -1.7228683861943337

#% cell
n(cosh_integral(2), 30)
#% output
#= 2.4526669226469145219061326474994929

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(cosh_integral(x), x)
#% output
#= cosh(x)/x

#% text
# `Shi + Chi` is `Ei`:

#% cell
sinh_integral(1.5) + cosh_integral(1.5) - exp_integral_ei(1.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sinh_integral`, `cos_integral`, `exp_integral_ei`
